/Alt (Flowchart illustrating the mechanisms of diabetic cardiomyopathy. It shows Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus \(T2DM\) linked to a high-sugar, high-fat diet, contributing to 90% of cases, and Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus \(T1DM\) related to autoimmune insulin deficiency, contributing 10%. High blood sugar leads to reactive oxygen species \(ROS\) and 4-HNE formation, impacting heart health. Different cellular components and processes involved, such as membrane permeabilization, transport disorder, and metabolic reprogramming, are shown affecting mitochondria, lysosomes, and the Golgi apparatus. Key phrases describe various disruptions and failures within these systems.)
