266 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating the process of membrane permeabilization leading to cell death. It shows interactions between 4-HNE, LMP, and CDC, with effects like decreased enzyme activity, autophagic flux blockade, and autophagosome volumetric stress. These lead to cell death and ferroptosis through Fenton reaction involving NCOA4, GPX4, and ACSL4. Key processes and molecules such as TFEB and LAMP-2A are highlighted.)
